Yes. Since Agent Dhara has a complex backend with assessment agents, specialist chat agents, compiler stages, validation, execution, and improvement tracking, the UI should not expose that complexity as one long technical form.

The UI should behave like a guided data-engineering workspace:

Select data → Assess quality → Review findings → Define transformations → Estimate cost → Generate pipeline → Validate → Execute → Monitor improvement

