8. State handling is critical

The UI should not keep the complete pipeline only inside page.tsx React state. That could cause state loss after refresh or navigation.

Use one persistent pipeline context:

type PipelineContext = {
  sessionId: string;
  projectId: string;
  currentStage: string;
  selectedSources: SelectedSource[];
  assessmentResult?: AssessmentResult;
  businessRules: BusinessRule[];
  approvedSemantics: SemanticAction[];
  transformationPlan?: TransformationPlan;
  compilerOptions?: CompilerOptions;
  deploymentPackageId?: string;
  executionStatus?: ExecutionStatus;
};


Persist the important state in the backend session store:

Selected sources
Assessment job ID
Assessment results
Approved rules
Semantic actions
Compiler target
Cost estimate
Artifact package ID
Execution approval
Latest run ID

The frontend can cache this state, but the backend should remain the source of truth.

