10. What to avoid
Avoid one giant wizard page

If everything remains in app/data-pipeline/page.tsx, it will eventually become hard to manage. Break it into stage containers and reusable components.

Avoid showing every agent as a separate page

Users care about outcomes, not the number of agents. Reflect agent activity through progress, evidence, recommendations, and audit trails.

Avoid mixing recommendations with approved actions

Clearly distinguish:

Agent recommended
User approved
System executed


Use different status badges for each.

Avoid automatic execution after code generation

Compilation, validation, and execution should remain separate. Execution should require explicit approval.

Avoid hiding failures behind generic messages

Instead of:

Something went wrong.


show:

Compilation blocked during schema validation.

Column: CustomerID
Expected type: integer
Detected type: string
Suggested action: Add a cast transformation

Avoid requiring users to understand backend terminology

For example, display:

“Generated code does not match the selected database syntax.”

Then provide the technical detail:

DIALECT_VALIDATION_FAILED: NVL is unsupported for SQL Server.

